{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — at the beginning of my prayer, that You guide me in the path of Your righteousness." "<b>because of those who watch</b> — for I fear lest my foot slip and You punish me; then my watchers will rejoice and taste from the decree against us. And it is not close, like the enemy of David who look on the day of evil." "<b>And the word ha-yashar</b> — like: ha-yotze etcha (those who go out with you [Deut. 23:10])."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The phrase 'טעמו מגזרת אשורנו' (they will taste from the decree against us) is opaque; translated hyper-literally. The syntax of the final clause 'ולא קרוב כמו עוין את דוד המסתכלים' is difficult and possibly corrupt; rendered literally without emendation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:19.271272609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}